# French A2 — elementary vocabulary
#
# Words an A2 learner needs for the level's themes, in 16 categories so they can
# be shared out over the level's ten units. Nothing here is taught by an A1
# lesson (`words:` in data/curriculum/french/a1/lessons) or listed at another
# level. Examples may use A2 grammar (passé composé, imparfait, futur proche and
# simple, object pronouns, comparisons) and contain the word exactly as listed,
# never straight after l' or d', so the guided path can blank it out.
#
# Format: word | translations (semicolon-separated) | example sentence | category | difficulty (1-5) | example in English

# Travel, holidays and hotels — travel
voyage | trip; journey | Le voyage en train dure trois heures. | travel | 2 | The train journey takes three hours.
vacances | holidays; vacation | Nous partons en vacances la semaine prochaine. | travel | 2 | We're going on holiday next week.
valise | suitcase | J'ai fait ma valise hier soir. | travel | 2 | I packed my suitcase last night.
billet | ticket | J'ai acheté le billet sur internet. | travel | 2 | I bought the ticket online.
retard | delay | Le vol a deux heures de retard. | travel | 3 | The flight is two hours late.
réserver | to book; to reserve | Il faut réserver l'hôtel avant juillet. | travel | 3 | You have to book the hotel before July.
réservation | booking; reservation | J'ai une réservation au nom de Martin. | travel | 3 | I have a booking in the name of Martin.
annuler | to cancel | Je voudrais annuler ma réservation. | travel | 3 | I'd like to cancel my booking.
passeport | passport | N'oublie pas ton passeport pour le voyage. | travel | 2 | Don't forget your passport for the trip.
carte | map; card; menu | Regarde la carte, on est perdus. | travel | 2 | Look at the map, we're lost.
plan | street map; plan | J'ai pris un plan de la ville à l'hôtel. | travel | 3 | I picked up a map of the town at the hotel.
touriste | tourist | Ce touriste cherche le chemin du musée. | travel | 2 | This tourist is looking for the way to the museum.
guide | guide; guidebook | Le guide nous a montré la vieille ville. | travel | 2 | The guide showed us the old town.
séjour | stay | Notre séjour à Nice a duré une semaine. | travel | 3 | Our stay in Nice lasted a week.
réception | reception (desk) | Laissez la clé à la réception, s'il vous plaît. | travel | 3 | Leave the key at reception, please.
frontière | border | Nous avons passé la frontière en voiture. | travel | 3 | We crossed the border by car.
douane | customs | On a attendu une heure à la douane. | travel | 3 | We waited an hour at customs.
bagages | luggage; bags | Où est-ce que je peux laisser mes bagages ? | travel | 2 | Where can I leave my luggage?
sac à dos | backpack; rucksack | J'ai mis mon pull dans mon sac à dos. | travel | 2 | I put my jumper in my backpack.
camping | campsite; camping | Cet été, nous sommes allés au camping. | travel | 2 | This summer we went to a campsite.
tente | tent | On a dormi sous la tente au bord du lac. | travel | 2 | We slept in a tent by the lake.
auberge de jeunesse | youth hostel | Une nuit dans cette auberge de jeunesse coûte vingt euros. | travel | 3 | A night in this youth hostel costs twenty euros.
souvenir | souvenir; memory | J'ai acheté un souvenir pour ma sœur. | travel | 2 | I bought a souvenir for my sister.
château | castle | Nous avons visité un vieux château. | travel | 2 | We visited an old castle.
célèbre | famous | La tour Eiffel est très célèbre. | travel | 2 | The Eiffel Tower is very famous.
vue | view | De notre chambre, on avait une belle vue sur la mer. | travel | 2 | From our room we had a lovely view of the sea.
complet | full; fully booked | Désolé, l'hôtel est complet ce soir. | travel | 3 | Sorry, the hotel is full tonight.
départ | departure | Le départ est à huit heures précises. | travel | 2 | Departure is at eight o'clock sharp.
arrivée | arrival | Appelle-moi à ton arrivée à Paris. | travel | 2 | Call me when you get to Paris.
crème solaire | sun cream; sunscreen | N'oublie pas la crème solaire, il fait chaud. | travel | 2 | Don't forget the sun cream, it's hot.

# Getting around — transportation
aéroport | airport | Cet aéroport est loin du centre-ville. | transportation | 2 | This airport is a long way from the town centre.
quai | platform | Le train part du quai numéro trois. | transportation | 3 | The train leaves from platform three.
tourner | to turn | Au feu, il faut tourner à droite. | transportation | 2 | At the lights, you have to turn right.
traverser | to cross | Attends le feu vert pour traverser la rue. | transportation | 2 | Wait for the green light to cross the street.
arrêt | stop (bus, tram) | Je descends au prochain arrêt. | transportation | 2 | I'm getting off at the next stop.
feu | traffic light; fire | Le feu est rouge, il faut attendre. | transportation | 2 | The light is red, you have to wait.
carrefour | crossroads; junction | Tournez à gauche au carrefour. | transportation | 3 | Turn left at the crossroads.
parking | car park; parking lot | Le parking de la gare est payant. | transportation | 2 | You have to pay in the station car park.
essence | petrol; gasoline | Il y a une station essence après le pont. | transportation | 3 | There's a petrol station after the bridge.
permis | licence; permit | Mon frère a eu son permis à dix-huit ans. | transportation | 3 | My brother got his driving licence at eighteen.
rapide | fast; quick | Le train est plus rapide que le bus. | transportation | 2 | The train is faster than the bus.
lent | slow | Ce bus est vraiment lent. | transportation | 2 | This bus is really slow.
route | road | La route est dangereuse quand il neige. | transportation | 2 | The road is dangerous when it snows.
autoroute | motorway; highway | Cette autoroute va jusqu'à Marseille. | transportation | 3 | This motorway goes all the way to Marseille.
pont | bridge | Après le pont, tournez à gauche. | transportation | 2 | After the bridge, turn left.
tout droit | straight ahead | Continuez tout droit jusqu'à la poste. | transportation | 2 | Go straight on as far as the post office.
coin | corner | La pharmacie est au coin de la rue. | transportation | 2 | The pharmacy is on the corner of the street.
en face de | opposite; across from | La banque est en face de la gare. | transportation | 2 | The bank is opposite the station.
station | station (metro); resort | La station de métro est juste à côté. | transportation | 2 | The metro station is just next door.
correspondance | connection; change (of train) | J'ai raté ma correspondance à Lyon. | transportation | 3 | I missed my connection in Lyon.
aller-retour | return ticket; round trip | Un aller-retour pour Lille, s'il vous plaît. | transportation | 3 | A return ticket to Lille, please.
guichet | ticket office; counter | Achète ton billet au guichet. | transportation | 3 | Buy your ticket at the ticket office.
moto | motorbike | Mon cousin a acheté une moto rouge. | transportation | 2 | My cousin bought a red motorbike.
embouteillage | traffic jam | Il y a un embouteillage sur l'autoroute. | transportation | 3 | There's a traffic jam on the motorway.
circulation | traffic | Il y a beaucoup de circulation le vendredi soir. | transportation | 3 | There's a lot of traffic on Friday evenings.
garer | to park | Où est-ce que je peux garer la voiture ? | transportation | 3 | Where can I park the car?
panne | breakdown | Notre voiture est tombée en panne hier. | transportation | 3 | Our car broke down yesterday.

# Food, cooking and restaurants — food
boisson | drink | Qu'est-ce que tu veux comme boisson ? | food | 2 | What would you like to drink?
sel | salt | Il manque un peu de sel dans la soupe. | food | 2 | The soup needs a bit more salt.
beurre | butter | Passe-moi le beurre, s'il te plaît. | food | 2 | Pass me the butter, please.
boulanger | baker | Le boulanger prépare le pain chaque matin. | food | 2 | The baker makes the bread every morning.
cuisinier | cook | Mon oncle est cuisinier dans un grand restaurant. | food | 3 | My uncle is a cook in a big restaurant.
menu | set menu; menu | Le menu du jour coûte quinze euros. | food | 2 | The set menu of the day costs fifteen euros.
plat | dish; main course | Comme plat, je vais prendre le poulet. | food | 2 | For my main course, I'll have the chicken.
entrée | starter; entrance | Comme entrée, je voudrais une salade. | food | 2 | As a starter, I'd like a salad.
soupe | soup | Ma grand-mère fait une soupe aux légumes. | food | 2 | My grandmother makes vegetable soup.
pourboire | tip | On a laissé un pourboire au serveur. | food | 3 | We left the waiter a tip.
recette | recipe | Tu peux me donner la recette de ce gâteau ? | food | 2 | Can you give me the recipe for this cake?
farine | flour | Il faut deux cents grammes de farine. | food | 3 | You need two hundred grams of flour.
huile | oil | Cette huile d'olive vient d'Italie. | food | 3 | This olive oil comes from Italy.
poivre | pepper | Tu peux me passer le poivre ? | food | 2 | Can you pass me the pepper?
riz | rice | Ce soir, on mange du riz avec du poulet. | food | 2 | Tonight we're having rice with chicken.
jambon | ham | Je voudrais un sandwich au jambon. | food | 2 | I'd like a ham sandwich.
sauce | sauce | Cette sauce tomate est délicieuse. | food | 2 | This tomato sauce is delicious.
tomate | tomato | Coupe la tomate en petits morceaux. | food | 2 | Cut the tomato into small pieces.
carotte | carrot | Le lapin mange une carotte. | food | 2 | The rabbit is eating a carrot.
citron | lemon | Je voudrais un thé au citron. | food | 2 | I'd like a lemon tea.
confiture | jam | Je mets de la confiture sur mon pain. | food | 2 | I put jam on my bread.
cuire | to cook; to bake | Il faut cuire le gâteau trente minutes. | food | 3 | You have to bake the cake for thirty minutes.
couper | to cut | Tu peux couper le pain, s'il te plaît ? | food | 2 | Can you cut the bread, please?
goûter | to taste; afternoon snack | Tu veux goûter ma soupe ? | food | 3 | Do you want to taste my soup?
four | oven | Mets le gâteau au four pendant une demi-heure. | food | 3 | Put the cake in the oven for half an hour.
assiette | plate | Ton assiette est encore pleine. | food | 2 | Your plate is still full.
fourchette | fork | Il me manque une fourchette. | food | 2 | I'm missing a fork.
couteau | knife | Ce couteau ne coupe pas bien. | food | 2 | This knife doesn't cut well.
cuillère | spoon | Le bébé mange avec une petite cuillère. | food | 2 | The baby eats with a little spoon.
végétarien | vegetarian | Mon frère est végétarien depuis un an. | food | 3 | My brother has been a vegetarian for a year.
sucré | sweet | Ce gâteau est trop sucré pour moi. | food | 3 | This cake is too sweet for me.
salé | salty; savoury | Ce plat est un peu trop salé. | food | 3 | This dish is a bit too salty.

# Shops and money — shopping
prix | price | Le prix est écrit sur l'étiquette. | shopping | 2 | The price is on the label.
caisse | checkout; till | Payez à la caisse, s'il vous plaît. | shopping | 3 | Please pay at the till.
reçu | receipt | Gardez le reçu pour l'échange. | shopping | 3 | Keep the receipt in case you exchange it.
carte bancaire | bank card | On peut payer par carte bancaire ? | shopping | 3 | Can we pay by card?
espèces | cash | Je préfère payer en espèces. | shopping | 3 | I prefer to pay in cash.
soldes | sales | Les soldes commencent en janvier. | shopping | 3 | The sales start in January.
réduction | discount | Il y a une réduction de vingt pour cent. | shopping | 3 | There's a twenty per cent discount.
cher | expensive; dear | Cet hôtel est trop cher pour nous. | shopping | 2 | This hotel is too expensive for us.
bon marché | cheap; inexpensive | Ce restaurant est bon marché. | shopping | 3 | This restaurant is cheap.
monnaie | change (coins); currency | Je n'ai pas de monnaie pour le parking. | shopping | 3 | I haven't got any change for the car park.
portefeuille | wallet | J'ai perdu mon portefeuille dans le bus. | shopping | 3 | I lost my wallet on the bus.
rembourser | to refund; to pay back | Est-ce que vous pouvez me rembourser ? | shopping | 3 | Can you give me a refund?
échanger | to exchange | Je voudrais échanger ce pull contre un autre. | shopping | 3 | I'd like to exchange this jumper for another one.
panier | basket | J'ai mis les pommes dans le panier. | shopping | 2 | I put the apples in the basket.
centre commercial | shopping centre; mall | Samedi, nous sommes allés au centre commercial. | shopping | 2 | On Saturday we went to the shopping centre.
épicerie | grocer's; corner shop | Cette épicerie ferme très tard. | shopping | 3 | This grocer's closes very late.
librairie | bookshop | J'ai acheté ce livre à la librairie. | shopping | 3 | I bought this book at the bookshop.
commande | order | Ma commande est arrivée ce matin. | shopping | 3 | My order arrived this morning.
livraison | delivery | La livraison est gratuite le week-end. | shopping | 3 | Delivery is free at the weekend.
gratuit | free (no charge) | Le musée est gratuit pour les enfants. | shopping | 2 | The museum is free for children.
dépenser | to spend (money) | Je ne veux pas dépenser trop d'argent. | shopping | 3 | I don't want to spend too much money.
économiser | to save (money) | Je dois économiser pour acheter un vélo. | shopping | 3 | I have to save up to buy a bike.
queue | queue; line; tail | On a fait la queue pendant une heure. | shopping | 3 | We queued for an hour.
produit | product | Ce produit est fabriqué en France. | shopping | 3 | This product is made in France.

# Clothes — clothing
taille | size | Vous faites quelle taille en pantalon ? | clothing | 2 | What size are you in trousers?
essayer | to try; to try on | Je peux essayer cette veste ? | clothing | 2 | Can I try on this jacket?
vêtement | item of clothing; garment | Ce vêtement est trop petit pour moi. | clothing | 2 | This piece of clothing is too small for me.
veste | jacket | Cette veste te va très bien. | clothing | 2 | That jacket really suits you.
manteau | coat | J'ai laissé mon manteau dans l'entrée. | clothing | 2 | I left my coat in the hall.
ceinture | belt | J'ai perdu ma ceinture en cuir. | clothing | 3 | I've lost my leather belt.
chapeau | hat | Mets un chapeau, il y a du soleil. | clothing | 2 | Put a hat on, it's sunny.
pointure | shoe size | Quelle est votre pointure ? | clothing | 3 | What's your shoe size?
cabine d'essayage | fitting room | La cabine d'essayage est au fond du magasin. | clothing | 3 | The fitting room is at the back of the shop.
écharpe | scarf | Mets ton écharpe, il fait froid. | clothing | 2 | Put your scarf on, it's cold.
bonnet | woolly hat; beanie | En hiver, je porte un bonnet. | clothing | 2 | In winter I wear a woolly hat.
casquette | cap | Mon frère porte toujours une casquette. | clothing | 2 | My brother always wears a cap.
short | shorts | Il fait chaud, mets un short. | clothing | 2 | It's hot, put some shorts on.
baskets | trainers; sneakers | J'ai acheté des baskets pour courir. | clothing | 2 | I bought some trainers for running.
bottes | boots | Mets tes bottes, il y a de la boue. | clothing | 2 | Put your boots on, it's muddy.
pyjama | pyjamas | Mon petit frère est déjà en pyjama. | clothing | 2 | My little brother is already in his pyjamas.
lunettes | glasses | Je ne vois rien sans mes lunettes. | clothing | 2 | I can't see anything without my glasses.
montre | watch | Ma montre ne marche plus. | clothing | 2 | My watch has stopped working.
poche | pocket | J'ai mis mes clés dans ma poche. | clothing | 2 | I put my keys in my pocket.
coton | cotton | Ce t-shirt est en coton. | clothing | 3 | This T-shirt is made of cotton.
serré | tight | Ce pantalon est trop serré. | clothing | 3 | These trousers are too tight.
large | loose; wide; baggy | Cette chemise est un peu large. | clothing | 3 | This shirt is a bit loose.
court | short | Ton short est trop court. | clothing | 2 | Your shorts are too short.
mode | fashion | Ma sœur suit toujours la mode. | clothing | 3 | My sister always follows fashion.
enlever | to take off; to remove | Tu peux enlever tes chaussures ici. | clothing | 3 | You can take your shoes off here.

# Health and the body — health
fièvre | fever; temperature | J'ai de la fièvre depuis ce matin. | health | 3 | I've had a temperature since this morning.
rhume | cold (illness) | J'ai attrapé un rhume. | health | 3 | I've caught a cold.
maladie | illness; disease | Cette maladie est très rare. | health | 3 | This illness is very rare.
ordonnance | prescription | Le médecin m'a donné une ordonnance. | health | 3 | The doctor gave me a prescription.
pharmacie | pharmacy; chemist's | La pharmacie est ouverte la nuit. | health | 2 | The pharmacy is open at night.
œil | eye | Il a un œil tout rouge ce matin. | health | 2 | One of his eyes is all red this morning.
dos | back | J'ai mal au dos depuis hier. | health | 2 | My back has hurt since yesterday.
ventre | stomach; belly | J'ai mal au ventre après le repas. | health | 2 | I have a stomach ache after the meal.
dent | tooth | J'ai mal à une dent depuis lundi. | health | 2 | I've had toothache since Monday.
cou | neck | Il porte une écharpe autour du cou. | health | 2 | He's wearing a scarf round his neck.
épaule | shoulder | Mon épaule me fait mal depuis le match. | health | 3 | My shoulder has hurt since the match.
genou | knee | Je suis tombé et je me suis fait mal au genou. | health | 2 | I fell over and hurt my knee.
doigt | finger | Je me suis coupé le doigt avec un couteau. | health | 2 | I cut my finger with a knife.
gorge | throat | J'ai mal à la gorge quand je parle. | health | 2 | My throat hurts when I talk.
cœur | heart | Mon cœur bat très vite. | health | 2 | My heart is beating very fast.
peau | skin | Ma peau est toute rouge après la plage. | health | 3 | My skin is all red after the beach.
cheville | ankle | Elle s'est fait mal à la cheville. | health | 3 | She hurt her ankle.
corps | body | Le sport est bon pour le corps. | health | 2 | Sport is good for the body.
tousser | to cough | Il n'arrête pas de tousser depuis hier. | health | 3 | He hasn't stopped coughing since yesterday.
douleur | pain | J'ai une douleur dans le bras. | health | 3 | I have a pain in my arm.
se sentir | to feel | Il commence à se sentir mieux. | health | 3 | He's starting to feel better.
guérir | to get better; to heal | Tu vas vite guérir, ne t'inquiète pas. | health | 3 | You'll soon get better, don't worry.
rendez-vous | appointment; date | J'ai rendez-vous chez le dentiste demain. | health | 2 | I've got a dentist's appointment tomorrow.
urgences | A&E; emergency room | On a emmené mon frère aux urgences. | health | 3 | We took my brother to A&E.
ambulance | ambulance | Une ambulance est arrivée très vite. | health | 2 | An ambulance arrived very quickly.
comprimé | tablet; pill | Prenez un comprimé trois fois par jour. | health | 3 | Take one tablet three times a day.
pansement | plaster; bandage | Mets un pansement sur ton doigt. | health | 3 | Put a plaster on your finger.
blessure | injury; wound | Il a une petite blessure au genou. | health | 3 | He has a small injury on his knee.
allergie | allergy | J'ai une allergie aux chats. | health | 3 | I'm allergic to cats.
en forme | fit; in good shape | Je me sens en forme aujourd'hui. | health | 2 | I feel in good shape today.
grave | serious | Ne t'inquiète pas, ce n'est pas grave. | health | 2 | Don't worry, it's not serious.

# The home and chores — housing
immeuble | block of flats; apartment building | J'habite dans un immeuble de six étages. | housing | 3 | I live in a six-storey block of flats.
salle | room; hall | La salle de classe est grande et lumineuse. | housing | 3 | The classroom is big and bright.
escalier | stairs; staircase | Attention, cet escalier est dangereux. | housing | 3 | Careful, these stairs are dangerous.
ascenseur | lift; elevator | Notre immeuble a un ascenseur. | housing | 3 | Our building has a lift.
meuble | piece of furniture | Ce meuble vient de chez ma grand-mère. | housing | 3 | This piece of furniture came from my grandmother's.
placard | cupboard; closet | Les verres sont dans le placard. | housing | 3 | The glasses are in the cupboard.
loyer | rent | Je paie le loyer au début du mois. | housing | 3 | I pay the rent at the start of the month.
côté | side | Assieds-toi à côté de moi. | housing | 2 | Sit next to me.
pièce | room; coin; play | Le salon est la plus grande pièce de la maison. | housing | 2 | The living room is the biggest room in the house.
balcon | balcony | On prend le petit-déjeuner sur le balcon. | housing | 2 | We have breakfast on the balcony.
lumière | light | Tu peux allumer la lumière, s'il te plaît ? | housing | 2 | Can you turn the light on, please?
armoire | wardrobe | Cette armoire est trop grande pour ma chambre. | housing | 3 | This wardrobe is too big for my bedroom.
tiroir | drawer | Les cuillères sont dans le tiroir. | housing | 3 | The spoons are in the drawer.
lave-vaisselle | dishwasher | Mets les assiettes dans le lave-vaisselle. | housing | 3 | Put the plates in the dishwasher.
machine à laver | washing machine | La machine à laver est en panne. | housing | 3 | The washing machine has broken down.
louer | to rent; to hire | Nous voulons louer un appartement près du centre. | housing | 3 | We want to rent a flat near the centre.
déménager | to move (house) | Nous allons déménager à Lyon cet été. | housing | 3 | We're going to move to Lyon this summer.
bruit | noise | Il y a trop de bruit dans la rue. | housing | 2 | There's too much noise in the street.
confortable | comfortable | Ce canapé est très confortable. | housing | 2 | This sofa is very comfortable.
propre | clean; own | Ma chambre est enfin propre. | housing | 2 | My bedroom is clean at last.
sale | dirty | Ton pantalon est sale, mets-le dans la machine. | housing | 2 | Your trousers are dirty, put them in the machine.
ménage | housework; cleaning | Le samedi, je fais le ménage avec mon père. | housing | 3 | On Saturdays I do the cleaning with my dad.
vaisselle | dishes; washing-up | C'est ton tour de faire la vaisselle. | housing | 2 | It's your turn to do the washing-up.
lessive | laundry; washing | Ma mère fait la lessive le dimanche. | housing | 3 | My mother does the washing on Sundays.
nettoyer | to clean | Il faut nettoyer la salle de bain. | housing | 2 | The bathroom needs cleaning.
aspirateur | vacuum cleaner | Cet aspirateur fait beaucoup de bruit. | housing | 3 | This vacuum cleaner makes a lot of noise.
poubelle | bin; rubbish | Tu peux sortir la poubelle, s'il te plaît ? | housing | 2 | Can you take the bin out, please?
arroser | to water | Tu peux arroser les plantes ce week-end ? | housing | 3 | Can you water the plants this weekend?
débarrasser | to clear (the table) | Aide-moi à débarrasser la table. | housing | 3 | Help me clear the table.
laver | to wash | Je dois laver mon t-shirt préféré. | housing | 2 | I need to wash my favourite T-shirt.

# Work — work
réunion | meeting | La réunion commence à dix heures. | work | 3 | The meeting starts at ten.
entreprise | company; firm | Cette entreprise a cinquante employés. | work | 3 | This company has fifty employees.
chef | boss; head; chef | Le chef est en congé cette semaine. | work | 2 | The boss is on leave this week.
congé | leave; time off | Je prends deux semaines de congé en août. | work | 3 | I'm taking two weeks off in August.
emploi | job; employment | Il a trouvé un nouvel emploi. | work | 3 | He's found a new job.
entretien | interview; maintenance | J'ai un entretien d'embauche jeudi. | work | 3 | I have a job interview on Thursday.
stage | internship; work placement | J'ai fait un stage dans une banque. | work | 3 | I did an internship at a bank.
CV | CV; résumé | J'ai envoyé mon CV à trois entreprises. | work | 3 | I sent my CV to three companies.
employé | employee | Cet employé travaille ici depuis dix ans. | work | 3 | This employee has worked here for ten years.
usine | factory | Mon oncle travaille dans une usine. | work | 3 | My uncle works in a factory.
chômage | unemployment | Il est au chômage depuis trois mois. | work | 3 | He's been out of work for three months.
retraite | retirement | Ma grand-mère est à la retraite. | work | 3 | My grandmother is retired.
embaucher | to hire; to take on | L'entreprise va embaucher deux personnes. | work | 3 | The company is going to take on two people.
projet | project; plan | Nous avons un nouveau projet au travail. | work | 2 | We have a new project at work.
pause | break | On prend une pause de quinze minutes. | work | 2 | We take a fifteen-minute break.
avocat | lawyer; avocado | Il veut devenir avocat plus tard. | work | 3 | He wants to be a lawyer when he grows up.
informaticien | IT specialist; programmer | Mon père est informaticien à Lyon. | work | 3 | My dad works in IT in Lyon.
plombier | plumber | On a appelé le plombier pour la douche. | work | 3 | We called the plumber about the shower.
boulot | job; work (informal) | Je commence le boulot à neuf heures. | work | 3 | I start work at nine.
contrat | contract | J'ai signé mon contrat hier. | work | 3 | I signed my contract yesterday.
signer | to sign | Vous devez signer ce document. | work | 3 | You have to sign this document.
document | document | Imprime ce document pour la réunion. | work | 2 | Print this document for the meeting.
responsable | manager; person in charge | Je voudrais parler au responsable. | work | 3 | I'd like to speak to the manager.
télétravail | working from home; remote work | Je fais du télétravail le vendredi. | work | 3 | I work from home on Fridays.

# School and studying — education
cours | class; lesson | Le cours de piano dure une heure. | education | 2 | The piano lesson lasts an hour.
examen | exam | J'ai réussi mon examen d'histoire. | education | 2 | I passed my history exam.
devoirs | homework | J'ai beaucoup de devoirs à faire ce soir. | education | 2 | I have a lot of homework to do tonight.
note | mark; grade; note | J'ai eu une bonne note en maths. | education | 2 | I got a good mark in maths.
dictionnaire | dictionary | Cherche ce mot dans le dictionnaire. | education | 2 | Look this word up in the dictionary.
difficile | difficult; hard | Cet exercice est trop difficile pour moi. | education | 2 | This exercise is too hard for me.
facile | easy | Le contrôle était très facile. | education | 2 | The test was very easy.
