# Useful verbs — verbs
se reposer | to rest | Le dimanche, mon père aime se reposer. | verbs | 2 | On Sundays my dad likes to rest.
se dépêcher | to hurry | Il faut se dépêcher, le train va partir ! | verbs | 3 | We need to hurry, the train is about to leave!
s'endormir | to fall asleep | Mon petit frère n'arrive pas à s'endormir. | verbs | 3 | My little brother can't get to sleep.
rencontrer | to meet | J'aimerais rencontrer tes parents. | verbs | 2 | I'd like to meet your parents.
retrouver | to meet up with; to find again | On va retrouver nos amis au café. | verbs | 3 | We're going to meet our friends at the café.
passer | to spend (time); to pass; to drop in | Nous allons passer une semaine à Rome. | verbs | 2 | We're going to spend a week in Rome.
retourner | to go back; to return | Je voudrais retourner en Italie l'année prochaine. | verbs | 3 | I'd like to go back to Italy next year.
